     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in most labeling. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose**, or another dose you had in mind.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
